inserted by the injector → dropped.\n   * `hadm_id`: restored from the stay of `icu/icustays.csv`.\n   * `charttime`: events moved to `outtime + 1 day` are restored with the *chart\n     session* (all rows of one `(subject_id, stay_id, storetime)` share a chart time).\n3. **values**\n   * `icu/chartevents.valuenum`\n     * text valued rows (assessments/ordinals): the numeric code is a deterministic\n       function of `(itemid, value)`.  The code map is rebuilt from the majority\n       non-zero code of that pair; a pair without any non-zero code yields `0` only\n       when the zero codes outnumber the empty ones, otherwise the value stays empty.\n     * numeric valued rows: `valuenum` = the numeric value.\n     * MIMIC *native* errors (value == valuenum, physiologically impossible, ≥ 20 %\n       away from the patient's median for that item, and the patient has at least one\n       in-range reading) are replaced by the patient/item median.\n   * `icu/inputevents.amount`: the placeholder (`-888/-999/-1000/-1`) is replaced by\n     `originalamount` (fallback `totalamount`).\n   * `icu/inputevents.endtime`: the placeholder `starttime - 60 s` → `starttime + 60 s`.\n   * `icu/outputevents.charttime`: the unix epoch → the hour the event was stored in.\n   * `hosp/labevents.valuenum`: the raw `valuenum`, falling back to the numeric `value`\n     text column; `valueuom == 'N/A'` → empty.\n   * `hosp/diagnoses_icd.icd_code` / `hosp/procedures_icd.icd_code`: the `ALIAS_` prefix\n     is removed.\n   * `hosp/admissions.hospital_expire_flag`: recomputed from `discharge_location`/`deathtime`.\n   * `hosp/patients.gender`: recovered from the discharge note (`Sex: M/F`).\n4. **de-duplication** – identical raw rows are removed *after* the key column repairs.\n   De-duplicating after the value repair as well removes genuine MIMIC duplicates that\n   the reference keeps, so the de-duplication happens on the raw row (with the raw\n   `valuenum`) after the key repairs.\n5. **cohort** – hospital admissions of the ICU patients that have ICU medication\n   administration events (`icu/inputevents.csv`).  Every ICU stay of the raw slice is\n   kept in `icu/*`; the hospital level tables are restricted to the cohort.\n6. **ECG** – the studies whose `ecg_time` falls into an ICU stay window, joined with the\n   stay (`hadm_id`, `stay_id`, `intime`, `outtime`) and the constant waveform path.\n\n## Train self check\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/pipeline.py --raw-root <train_raw> --output-dir work/t_final\npython3 scripts/selfcheck.py --out-dir work/t_final --ref-dir <train_reference>\n```\n\nmean row precision 0.955, mean row recall 0.863, mean cell accuracy 0.908\n(per file: `work/train_selfcheck.json`).\n\nFiles that are reproduced exactly (row by row): `cohort.csv`, `diagnoses.csv`,\n`procedures.csv`, `medications.csv`, `labs.csv`, `icu/icustays.csv`.\n`icu/chartevents.csv`: 60 513 / 60 681 rows, cell accuracy 0.996.\n"}
