This round's feedback pinpointed the main defect. Here's what I found and fixed:

## Root cause: the cohort (7 of 13 files were wrong)

The gold cohort has **16** rows on validation, I produced 15 — and, more importantly, the hospital-level files had completely wrong row counts (labs 10 552 vs gold 5 765, medications 1 854 vs 1 249, diagnoses 325 vs 357, procedures 63 vs 56).

Re-deriving from the row counts proved the gold cohort = *the admissions minus exactly one patient*: `11 851 − 6 086 = 5 765` labs (the excluded patient has 6 086 lab rows), `396 − 39 = 357` diagnoses, `2 142 − 893 = 1 249` prescriptions. That patient is **not** a "missing ICU treatment events" case (my previous rule) but a patient whose **complete hospital record set was copied into the slice** by the injector.

It is detectable: a copied patient's hospital rows are wildly out of proportion to the ICU rows of the same stay —

| | copied patient | next highest real patient |
|---|---|---|
| train | 5 912 hosp / 716 ICU = **5.37** | 0.60 |
| validation | 20 370 hosp / 6 021 ICU = **2.17** | 0.82 |

New rule: cohort = admissions minus the subjects whose `hospital rows / ICU rows` ratio exceeds `max(1.5, 2×median)` → it reproduces the train reference cohort exactly (17025507 removed) and the validation cohort exactly (16965015 removed).

## Other fixes found by diffing against the raw/reference

| fix | evidence | effect |
|---|---|---|
| `stay_id` alias `9<id>` → `<id>` (2 274 chart rows train / 901 validation) | the row's `subject_id` no longer matches the stay | chartevents P 0.959→**0.991**, R 0.956→**0.988** |
| `ecg_measurements` must be ordered by `ecg_time` (the manifest by `(subject_id, study_id)`) | train reference row order | ecg_measurements 0.687 → ≈1.0 |
| `inputevents.endtime`: infusion duration = `originalamount/rate` (36 % exact) instead of a flat +60 s | train reference durations | inputevents cell acc 0.234→**0.309** |

I also tried and **reverted** a session-mode charttime repair (it cost 775 more rows than it fixed) and checked several amount/duration estimators (scaling by the median ratio does not help).

## Verification

* **Train self-check**: row P **0.9575** / R **0.865** / cell **0.9135** (was 0.955/0.863/0.908).
* **Validation row counts now match the gold exactly** for 12/13 files (admissions 16, cohort 16, demographics 16, diagnoses 357, procedures 56, medications 1 249, labs 5 765, icustays 20, inputevents 1 720, outputevents 1 053, ecg 11/11; chartevents 71 949 vs 72 017).
* **Replay** from a clean directory reproduces all 13 package files byte-for-byte.

Deliverables are in the agent workdir: `results/` (13 csv + `submission.json`), the same package mirrored at the root, `submission.json` (`schema_version=1`, `result_root="results"`, `replay.argv`), the updated `train_analysis.json` (new rule entries with train evidence) and `README.md`.[Model Usage] input=508525 output=1331 reason=completed

