Score improved 0.758 → **0.868**. This round I found and fixed one clear bug and refined the rules:

## The bug: ECG measurement schema shift (`ecg_measurements` stuck at 0.687)

The reference package's `ecg_measurements.csv` has **18** `report_` columns (`report_0..report_17`), but I had hard-coded 17 — so every column after the reports (`bandwidth`, `rr_interval`, `p_onset`, `p_axis`, …) was compared against the **wrong** column. The train slice has 17 report columns, the validation slice 18, i.e. the schema follows the raw table per slice (the same phenomenon as the ECG manifest, which already scored 1.0).

Fix: project the raw `ecg/machine_measurements.csv` schema as-is and append `hadm_id`/`stay_id`. Verified against the train reference: **identical column list, 0 differing cells** (previously 34 vs 35 columns).

## Rule refinements

| file | change | effect (train self-check) |
|---|---|---|
| `icu/inputevents.csv` | infusion duration = `originalamount / rate` (the injector had flattened every `endtime` to `starttime − 60 s`); boluses keep `starttime + 60 s` | cell accuracy 0.234 → **0.309** |
| `icu/chartevents.csv` | `stay_id` alias `9<id>` → `<id>` (2 274 train / 901 validation rows; detectable because the row's `subject_id` no longer matches the stay) | row P 0.959→**0.991**, R 0.956→**0.988**, multiset 0.94→**0.976** |
| cohort | already fixed last round (copied hospital records detected via the `hospital rows / ICU rows` outlier) | 7 of 13 files now at **1.000** |

